{title: Ive Been To The Potters House}
{key: G}
{x_theme: grace-mercy, altar, healing}
{x_source: chrd:ive_been_to_the_potters_house.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]Tossed about by life's battles
All my [F]hope was sinking [C]fast,
The sinful life that I was living
I [D]knew that I just could not [G]last.
Then I went [C]down to the Potter's house
And placed my [F]vessel into his hands
On His wheel of grace and [C]mercy
He made me [G]over [C]again.

{comment: Chorus}
Yes, I've [F]been to the Potter's house
His hands of [C]mercy molded me
He sat before when He was finished
So, that [D]all the world could [G]see,
That He can [C]mend a broken vessel
It matters [F]not what shape it's in,
Yes, I've [C]been to the Potter's house,
I've been made me [G]over [C]again.

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]If your life has no meaning
The [F]storms have taken their toll on [C]you,
With you vessel in many pieces
You [D]don't know just what to [G]do.
Please come [C]with me to the Potter's house
And place your [F]vessel into his hands
You'll be amazed at His [C]ability
When He molds [G]you  [C]again.
